          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/little+site"} little site
            notion of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zariski+topology"} Zariski topology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/big+site"} big site
            notion. As for the little site notion: the Zariski topology on the set of prime ideals of a commutative ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is the smallest topology that contains, as open sets, sets of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi p
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mtext prime
                  %mo :
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∉
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{p\; \text{prime}: a \notin p\}
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            ranges over elements of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            As for the big site notion, the
            %em Zariski topology
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CRing"} CRing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}^{op}
            of commutative rings. This article is mainly about the big site notion.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            a commutative
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi R
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi CRing
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec R \in CRing^{op}
            for its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+of+a+commutative+ring"} spectrum of a commutative ring
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
          #StandardOpenImmersion.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset R
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+subset"} multiplicative subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R[S^{-1}]
              for the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+ring"} localization
              and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Spec(R[S^{-1}]) \longrightarrow Spec(R)
            %p
              for the dual of the canonical ring homomorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \to R[S^{-1}]
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The maps as in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StandardOpenImmersion"}
              are not
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+immersion+of+schemes"} open immersions
              for arbitrary multiplicative subsets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              (see
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/20782/ring-theoretic-characterization-of-open-affines"} a MathOverflow discussion
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S = \{ f^0, f^1, f^2, \ldots \}
              %em standard opens
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spec
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(R)
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A family of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi Spec
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{Spec A_i \to Spec R\}
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing^{op}
              is a Zariski-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering"} covering
              precisely if
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  each ring
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_i
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msubsup
                          %mi r
                          %mi i
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        A_i = R[r_i^{-1}]
                %p
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
