                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntactic+category"} syntactic category
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+theory"} cartesian theory
                  of commutative rings;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi CRing
                          %mi fp
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing_{fp}^{op}
                  equipped with the Zariski topology is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntactic+site"} syntactic site
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+theory"} geometric theory
                  of
                  = succeed "s." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+ring"} local ring
            %p Hence
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the big Zariski topos, def.
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ZariskiTopos"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+topos"} classifying topos
                  for
                  = succeed "s." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+ring"} local ring
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+ringed+topos"} locally ringed topos
                  is equivalently a topos
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℰ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
                  equipped with a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
                  into the big Zariski topos.
          %p
            See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+topos"} classifying topos
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+ringed+topos"} locally ringed topos
